  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#serialize-a-color-well-control-color\n\n> 2. Round each of color's components so they are in the range 0 to 255, inclusive. Components are to be [rounded towards +∞](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#combine-integers).\n\nBut this is not happening in the actual WebKit implementation, nor it seems reasonable. If I set `hsl(150deg 150 53.5)` as the color and see the resulting RGB value, it's `#00ff88` in WebKit, while if it's rounded towards +infinity then the B value would be 0x89 (137 in decimal, rounded from 136.425).\n\nIt also doesn't seem to be the actual CSS behavior (if I set it to the page background color then I see 0x88 as the B value). So it should probably round to the nearest integer than towards +infinity.\n\ncc @annevk @emilio",
